# [SQUAD](../wg/squad.html)

## Summary

The SQUAD (Scalable QUIC Applications and Delivery) session at IETF 127 was a non-working-group-forming Birds of a Feather (BOF) session chaired by Lucas Pardue and Lenny Giuliani. The primary goal of the BOF was to explore whether there is community interest in addressing application delivery scalability by combining QUIC with IP multicast (or multicast routing architectures generally), to examine relevant deployment scenarios and technical challenges, and to collect feedback on potential next steps (such as dispatching work to existing working groups, creating a dedicated mailing list, or holding a working-group-forming BOF in the future).

The session featured six presentations covering the problem statement and boundaries, deployment scenarios (multicast ABR and 5G MBS), modern multicast routing developments (SSM, AMT, BIER), transport and congestion control considerations, implementation experience (Flexicast QUIC and MC-QUIC prototypes), and the integration of Media over QUIC (MoQ) over Multicast QUIC. An open discussion followed, focusing on wireless/Wi-Fi constraints, unicast vs. multicast capacity limits, application-transport boundaries, and whether the problem scope should be broadened beyond QUIC and IP multicast.

